0..70 Comment "// The comparisons `!=`, `<=` and `>=`, each deciding a `while` loop\'s"
71..148 Comment "// condition: the loop runs its body while the comparison holds, and the body"
149..223 Comment "// returns at once (the relational and equality operators of Kernighan and"
224..301 Comment "// Ritchie, _The C Programming Language_, 2nd ed., § 2.6). A `while` may run"
302..359 Comment "// forever, so each function states `Partial` in its row."
360..362 Comment "//"
363..378 Comment "// - see: #1481"
